 reviewed work in the linearizer prompt.
 
+When automatic review finishes cleanly for a user patch agent, the controller appends a
+feature-completion acknowledgement prompt to that patch-agent session and selects the patch chat so
+the answer is visible. A `yes` or `y` reply records the acknowledgement in the session transcript and
+marks the feature complete from the frontend's perspective; any other reply leaves normal follow-up
+chat routing available.
+
 The command transcript is also the conversation history for the persistent `command-agent`. That
 system agent interprets chat sent to the Work Leaf command surface. It recognizes literal command
 lines and common natural-language requests for help, review, linearization, quitting, and launching
@@ -305,6 +311,13 @@ state for that session. `TerminalUi` queues one terminal bell when a chat transi
 state and renders ready rows in reverse video so they remain highlighted until the chat becomes busy
 again.
 
+After a reviewed patch chat receives a positive feature-completion acknowledgement, the terminal app
+hides that patch-agent row from the left pane while keeping the reviewer row visible. Sending a later
+follow-up to the same patch chat locally reopens the hidden row, routes the message through the
+controller, and allows a later clean review to close the row again. The terminal cache preserves
+repeated acknowledgement prompts and completion lines so separate review cycles remain visible in
+the chat transcript.
+
 `src/ui.rs::TerminalUi` owns terminal-specific presentation state:
 
 - `UiMode`, `PaneFocus`, `UiSurface`, `UiKey`, and `UiAction` model terminal interactions.
